## Implementation Scope And Protected Work

Primary candidates are packages/control-ui/src/WorkStep.tsx, planned src/DocumentedApprovals.tsx and scoped src/style.css. Reuse src/presentation.ts documentName and existing App.tsx navigation/focus without a new owner. Do not alter Core, public DTOs, MCP/HTTP contracts, reader/session code or global configuration to make this presentation work. If inspection establishes a material change outside the approved design, stop dependent implementation and re-route before editing it.

Tests belong to existing packages/control-ui/test owners: planned documented-approvals.test.tsx and test/browser/documented-approvals.spec.mjs plus relevant existing work-step, scoped-reading, draft-check and browser journeys/scoped/changes/draft-check assertions. Preserve reader and security checks; do not weaken them to accommodate new labels. Existing build tools own any generated browser/MCP artefacts; inventory their actual paths separately and never hand-edit bundles. Use isolated fixtures and a qualified build directory so observation cannot replace another active host's assets.

T-001 captures the exact pre-existing dirty bytes/diffs of candidate and generated paths, including staged and untracked files, before code edits. Review this increment against that baseline rather than claiming the whole HEAD diff. Retain staged state and earlier work; no reset, clean, checkout or blanket overwrite. Rollback, if required, restores only this increment against the captured baseline through the scoped owner.

Protect this Run's approved UR/PRD/SD and histories; all artefacts/history of the completed cockpit-draft-check-integration-20261009-01; earlier backlog-status-flow-clarity-20261009-01 sources and independent decisions; all other Run artefacts. Selected-Run canonical writer transitions are recorded separately from product reading, which remains non-mutating. Test source changes occur only in isolated temporary fixture targets. MCP_CANDIDATES.md continues the user's observation assignment without authorizing candidate implementation.

## Scenario Definitions

- SCN-001: Zero, four and six canonical approved rows, including supported later gates, plus a non-approved row. Open the overview in compact and expanded placement. Verify actual count and exactly one row per approved gate, no fixed-four assumption, explicit empty state and document/evidence/version groups.
- SCN-002: Original evidence with long text, absent/blank evidence and misleading owner/date/path/partial-hash/signature-like prose. Details start closed; activate Dokumentiert. Preserve original text as text, show unsupported structured version/time/person/scope/basis explicitly unavailable or unconfirmed, retain recorded gate facts and one shared control-status explanation. No fabricated identity or certification; HTML-looking evidence cannot execute.
- SCN-003: Same-Run registered current resource with an unchanged path/digest and approved status. Activate its action: wording is Aktuelle Fassung ansehen; callback receives the exact Resource and approval:<resource_id> origin; actual reader opens captured current bytes. No Freigegebene Fassung ansehen from today's DTO.
- SCN-004: Change contents, rename/move the registered source through the fixture's existing registry, and include historic-looking partial hashes in evidence. Reload through the existing reader and open the new current resource. Actual bytes/identity agree with the current-version wording; no prose/path/digest match certifies a historical version. Old captured selectors remain subject to existing guards.
- SCN-005: Missing matching resource, unsupported/unregistered resource, foreign-Run matching gate, blocked source and sourceDisabled. Missing eligible resource yields an explicit unavailable state with no working action; disabled current actions cannot invoke onOpen. Count/evidence remain intact. Reader-owned blocked failures retain their existing feedback rather than pretending readable availability.
- SCN-006: Two registered same-Run resources match one approved gate. The row remains one recorded approval with explicitly identified current-resource actions; each action passes its own exact resource/origin. No silently selected first source and no invented historical distinction.
- SCN-007: In the actual built browser, use compact and expanded placements with wide and narrow available panel widths, Tab/Enter to open/close original evidence and activate a current-resource action. Accessible names distinguish repeated actions. Closing document returns focus to the initiating resource action and retains selected Run.
- SCN-008: Keep evidence open and focused while resizing the actual panel/container wide to narrow and back. Verify the same native details node, open state and action identity survive; long document/evidence text wraps, no horizontal overflow, targets stay usable and no competing responsive tree or focus trap appears. Scroll down/back with selection unchanged; ordinary resize causes reflow without unrelated list remount/jump/flicker.
- SCN-009: Reload while viewing this Run after guarded source change; exercise supported retry after a fixture-controlled transient reader failure and expired/stale source feedback. Old actions cannot bypass sourceDisabled/freshness; new selection/resources use existing owners. Return from reading and disclosure remains usable; no foreign Run appears.
- SCN-010: Around evidence open/close, document read/close and failed reads, snapshot fixture control/approval/source bytes and request endpoints. Bytes remain unchanged except explicit test setup; no gate writer, generic file/path call or new authoring-check request is triggered by these actions. Existing current-control assessment and draft-check action/results remain separate and usable.
- SCN-011: Record qualified browser and MCP UI bundle digests, source identity, supported Node/toolchain and exact command outcomes. Inspect captured narrow/wide/long/empty/additional-gate rendered cases and correlate screenshots with that build. Browser evidence does not stand in for native host proof.
- SCN-012: Compare actual incremental source/test/generated diff and protected artefact bytes against T-001. All six criteria and SD decisions have actual evidence; previous approved sources and other Run histories remain unchanged. Attribute any native observation to its actual build/runtime and limits; otherwise explicitly record absence. Required check failures remain blockers, not silently accepted evidence gaps.

