## Test Plan And Evidence Commands

Use the existing supported Node toolchain and existing installed dependencies. Record node --version, relevant source/lockfile identities and exact command/exit evidence. Planned suites are created only after T-001 permits implementation. Commands below are verification choices, not already executed results. Log failures completely and record compact pass evidence; do not repeat broad checks after success unless changes or unresolved findings justify it.

| Working directory | Planned command or observation | Purpose |
|---|---|---|
| packages/control-ui | npx vitest run test/documented-approvals.test.tsx test/work-step.test.tsx | Counts, original evidence, misleading prose, eligible resources, contextual controls and exact callback semantics |
| packages/control-ui | npx vitest run test/scoped-reading.test.tsx test/refresh-control.test.tsx test/mcp-changes.test.tsx | Existing selected-source/read/freshness/reload regressions |
| packages/control-ui | npx vitest run test/draft-check.test.tsx | Preserve neighboring draft-check behavior and its separate authority |
| packages/control-ui | npm run typecheck | Existing typed UI integration; no new public DTO |
| packages/control-ui | npm run build | Actual browser assets through established build, including existing prebuild tokens |
| packages/control-ui | npm run build:mcp | Actual self-contained MCP App build; record manifest, digest and generated scope |
| packages/control-ui | npm run test:browser -- test/browser/documented-approvals.spec.mjs test/browser/journeys.spec.mjs test/browser/scoped.spec.mjs test/browser/changes.spec.mjs test/browser/draft-check.spec.mjs | New actual rendered cases plus existing document, selection, freshness and draft-check journeys |
| Repository root | git diff --check plus comparison with captured candidate byte/diff baseline | Whitespace and attributable incremental scope; read-only Git inspection only |
| Selected Run evidence | Compare PROTECTED_SOURCES.json to actual post-change bytes; inspect screenshots and actual browser observations | Protected source/history and visibly verified hierarchy, wrapping and interaction |

Use the existing browser server-fixture production service and its AGDF_COCKPIT_TEST_DIST override with an isolated copied qualified build, avoiding replacement of another session's served files. New browser fixtures extend existing local fixture patterns and real document read flow; transport injection controls transient failure only, not invented certification or control authority. Capture requests/fixture byte comparisons for the no-write observation. Existing service/security implementations remain unchanged.

Required rendered widths: available content/panel widths approximately 320 CSS px and 960 CSS px, observed inside actual browser viewports 360 and 1280 CSS px. Measure the real approval container width; if surrounding chrome reduces it, resize the panel/viewport to obtain the intended narrow/wide cases and record actual measurements. Exercise compact and expanded placement, four normal rows, extra gates, empty state, long names/evidence, details open while resizing, keyboard navigation, return focus, scroll and reload. Check at least 44 CSS px usable interactive targets, document/panel horizontal overflow, same-node identity and readable relationships. Actual screenshots and browser inspection are required; DOM emulation alone is insufficient. Distinguish expected content-height reflow from unrelated list/selection jumps and retain failure traces/observations if instability occurs.

Any native observation is optional evidence under approved AC-006, with the actual build digest/runtime, observed actions and attribution recorded separately. An old installed Cockpit, the preceding Run's manual stability reply or a protocol advertisement proves nothing about this new UI. No install/config/restart is implicit. If the new qualified build is unavailable in the existing native host, write evidence/NATIVE_LIMITS.md explicitly; required browser/source/build evidence still applies. No universal platform or native-host claim is allowed.

## Risks, Dependencies And Stop Conditions

- Dirty preceding-scope files: T-001 must preserve exact prior bytes and staged/untracked state; unsafe attribution or protected-source change blocks completion.
- Historical proof absence: accepted current-version alternative is mandatory. Discovery of a new certification need returns to product/design routing; do not add archive, signature parsing or a new contract.
- Responsive density: shared general list spacing can recreate tall blocks; scoped CSS and actual rendered comparisons must establish the approved hierarchy, not just updated strings.
- Focus and multiple-resource ambiguity: exact existing resource/origin and stable native nodes are required; do not create a parallel navigation/focus store.
- Missing dependency/environment: record the failed check and next owner action. No automatic dependency upgrade, global configuration or approval waiver.
- A required failed/missing source, browser, build, scope or review check prevents a clean QA claim. Native absence is the approved explicitly reported limit and cannot hide a failed required browser check.

## Out Of Scope

No new Core/MCP function, public read protocol/DTO, persistent disclosure state, archive, certification, permission, gate writer or independent evaluator. No broad dashboard/backlog redesign, unrelated finding closure, changes to approved sources, global install/config, Git write, PR, publication or release action. MCP candidate recording is observational only.

